## Step 0.9a: Apple release boundary (report-only)

ECPE v1 has no reviewed App Store or TestFlight writer, pinned Xcode/fastlane
artifact contract, credential lifecycle, or response-loss reconciler. Inspect
the target and report prerequisites only.

An explicit Apple distribution request returns
`adapter_operation_unsupported` before any child or persistent write. It must
spawn zero package installs, sign-in/session commands, key minting, app-record
creation, pricing, upload, metadata, or submission operations. It must not
create `apple-effects.log`, `.gstack/apple/api-key.json`, fastlane state, store
assets, or any repository/home credential file.

There is no agentic browser of any kind, for any password, key, or token, under any framing.

Supporting Apple distribution requires a later reviewed closed provider
adapter. A resolve-only grant is forbidden because it would leave a raw tool as
the real writer.
